<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>What is RegexProof?</h3>
<p>RegexProof converts a natural-language description into a regex for the engine you choose, then explains it part by part and flags edge cases.</p>
<h3>Which regex flavors does RegexProof support?</h3>
<p>You choose the flavor — ECMAScript/JavaScript, PCRE, and others — and should validate against the production dialect, not only a paste-bin tester.</p>
<h3>How does RegexProof reduce ReDoS risk?</h3>
<p>It explains repetition and alternation and calls out patterns prone to catastrophic backtracking, the root cause of ReDoS (Regular-expression Denial of Service).</p>
<h3>Is RegexProof free?</h3>
<p>The Free tier includes 10 forges per month; Pro is $19/mo for higher volume.</p>
<h3>Why do ECMAScript and PCRE behave differently?</h3>
<p>Lookbehind support, Unicode modes, and recursive patterns differ across engines, so a pattern valid in PCRE can fail or act differently in JavaScript.</p>
